<title>THAILAND: Cambodia amends Shinawatra concession.</title>
<headline>Cambodia amends Shinawatra concession.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cambodian government has amended terms of a fixed telephone line concession held by Thai communications firm Shinawatra, a company statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Shinawatra Computer and Communication Plc's subsidiary Shinawatra International now holds 100 percent of the project up from 70 percent. The Cambodian government previously held 30 percent.</p>
<p>The length of the concession has been extended to 35 years from 15 years and allows the company to begin establishing a digital wireless network.</p>
<p>Shinawatra Computer and Communication Plc owns 80 percent of Shinawatra International.</p>
</text>
